      "Originally Enron Oil & Gas, separated from Enron in 1999 well before its collapse. Ezra Yacob has been CEO since 2021. EOG is one of the largest US independent oil and gas producers, concentrated in the Permian Basin, Eagle Ford and Delaware Basin. It built a reputation for capital discipline before the rest of the shale industry adopted it, focusing on returns per well rather than production growth — an approach that looked conservative for years and then looked prescient.",
