      "Spun out of ConocoPhillips in 2012, though the Phillips name dates to 1917. Mark Lashier has been CEO since 2022. Phillips 66 refines crude oil into petrol, diesel and jet fuel, operates midstream pipelines and storage, markets fuel through branded stations, and holds a 50% stake in the CPChem petrochemicals joint venture. Refining economics depend on the crack spread — the gap between crude cost and refined product prices — which is volatile and outside management control.",
