      [0.04, 0.05, 0.05, 0.04, 0.04], 0.24, 0.28, 0.080, 0.025,
      "Chartered by Congress in 1862 to build the eastern portion of the first transcontinental railroad. Jim Vena became CEO in 2023. Union Pacific operates around 32,000 route miles across the western two-thirds of the United States, hauling coal, grain, chemicals, industrial products and intermodal containers. It has agreed to acquire Norfolk Southern in an $85 billion deal that would add an eastern network; the transaction is under Surface Transportation Board review, with completion expected in the second half of 2027. Railroads are close to un-replicable — no one is building a competing transcontinental network — which gives the industry unusual structural pricing power.",
