      "Founded in 1963 by Ralph Roberts, whose son Brian Roberts has been CEO since 2002 and has shared the role with co-CEO Mike Cavanagh since January 2026. Comcast is the largest US cable broadband provider and owns NBCUniversal — the broadcast network, Universal film studio, theme parks and the Peacock streaming service. It completed the spin-off of Versant Media Group in January 2026, and the Epic Universe park opened in Orlando in 2025. Its central problem is that broadband, the profit engine, has stopped growing as fixed wireless and fibre competitors take share.",
